Development Task

You are part of Airtel's application development team.

The team has provided an existing Java project containing:

CustomerController
CustomerService
CustomerRepository
TicketController
TicketService
TicketRepository
Customer
ServiceTicket
TicketStatus

You need to enhance the application to support the new requirements while maintaining the existing functionality.

The implementation should include:

Customer lookup functionality
Ticket creation and update functionality
Input validation
Appropriate exception handling
REST API implementation
Unit tests for critical business logic
Meaningful comments and documentation
Consistent coding standards
Handling of invalid mobile numbers
Handling of customers who do not exist
Handling of duplicate tickets
Handling of invalid ticket-status transitions
Additional Scenario

The following request has been received from the Airtel operations team:

"If a customer reports that their network is unavailable, the service agent should be able to create a high-priority ticket. The system should automatically capture the customer information, issue description, current network status, and ticket creation timestamp."

The development team must implement this requirement without breaking the existing customer and ticket-management functionality.

Expected Outcome

At the end of the exercise, the candidate should provide a working enhancement to the existing application that:

Retrieves customer information correctly.
Creates and manages service tickets.
Handles invalid inputs gracefully.
Provides appropriate error messages.
Contains meaningful automated tests.
Follows the existing project's coding structure.
Includes documentation for the newly added functionality.
Can be maintained and extended by another developer.
